  "protocol": "Rule-engine benchmark, not a field-accuracy benchmark. There is no public corpus of annotated Indian GST invoices and the official rate sources (pib.gov.in, taxinformation.cbic.gov.in) could not be fetched, so no number here says whether our rate schedule is factually correct. Synthetic bills are generated from the schedule the engine is then judged against: part 1 tests longest-prefix lookup against an independent brute-force scan, part 2 perturbs a correct charged rate to each other legal slab and scores detection, part 3 sweeps a known paise error through the printed tax and reports the smallest error caught on every bill, part 4 confirms correctly built bills raise no GST failure. Rate correctness is out of scope and is declared unverified in the reference data.",
